ART Bay Area Sea Level Rise and Shoreline Analysis Maps (AECOM 2017 for BCDC/MTC), Alameda County geodatabase Alameda_SLR_ART_2017.gdb.zip (5315663176 bytes).
Source: https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/download.php, POST r=prep&f=Alameda_gdb then r=fetch, HTTP Range requests for the zip directory and the low-lying tables only.
Retrieved 2026-11-03T18:36:19Z. Rings whose bounding box meets the terrain grid plus 50 m are kept, coordinates EPSG:26910 rounded to 0.1 m.
Layer meaning (ART GIS data catalog, http://www.adaptingtorisingtides.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/GIS_data_catalog.pdf, p. 2): "These polygons identify low-lying areas greater than one acre. They depict areas that are below the inundated water surface elevation, but are not hydraulically-connected to the inundated areas."
